BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev_elissa_sail250-2026-08-09@coast-guide
DTSTAMP:20260809T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260809
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260810
SUMMARY:1877 Tall Ship ELISSA: free deck tours
DESCRIPTION:The ship is a National Historic Landmark\, a square-rigged iro
 n barque\, and one of only three ships of her kind left in the world that
  still actively sails. Pensacola is the first stop on her Sail250 voyage 
 for the nation's 250th. It is only her third recorded visit ever\, after 
 1886 and 2018. Walking her deck costs nothing. A ship-and-history kid get
 s rigging and 149 years of iron\, while the stroller rolls along the pier
 .\nPrice: Free\nArea: Pensacola\nTimes: Fri 8/7 – Sun 8/9 · free self-
 guided deck tours (hours vary by day · see watch-outs)\nChecked against 
 the venue's own page on 2026-08-05\nhttps://grayhicks.github.io/coast-gui
 de/events/ev-elissa-sail250.html
LOCATION:Palafox Pier\, 895 S Palafox St\, Pensacola\, FL 32502
URL:https://grayhicks.github.io/coast-guide/events/ev-elissa-sail250.html
END:VEVENT
